.\" rl man page
.TH RL 1 "2026-09-09" "rl 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rl \- the rl programming language toolchain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rl
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rl
is the command-line interface for the rl programming language. It provides
tools for running, checking, compiling, and packaging rl source files.
.PP
If no command is given and stdin is a terminal, the interactive REPL is started.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-\- " ARGS"]
Lex, parse, and evaluate a .rl source file. Arguments after the file path are
passed to the script as its argv.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-c ", \-\-code " CODE
Execute inline rl code instead of a file.
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Run through the bytecode VM.
.TP
.B \-\-cranelift
JIT compile via cranelift.
.RE
.TP
.B dev
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Run the current project by reading
.BR rl.toml .
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Run through the bytecode VM.
.TP
.B \-\-cranelift
JIT compile via cranelift.
.RE
.TP
.BI new " NAME"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Scaffold a new project directory or create a standalone script.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Skip running
.B git init
in the new project.
.TP
.B \-\-script
Create a standalone .rl script instead of a project directory.
.RE
.TP
.BI check " FILE"
Type-check a .rl file and report errors without running it.
.TP
.BI format " FILE"
Format a .rl source file in place.
.TP
.BI compile " FILE"
.RI [ \-o " OUTPUT"]
Lex, parse, resolve, and compile a .rl source file to .rlc bytecode.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-o ", \-\-output " PATH
Output .rlc path. Defaults to FILE with its extension changed to .rlc.
.RE
.TP
.BI print " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Print debug information for a .rl source file. Exactly one of
.BR \-\-tokens ", " \-\-parser ", " "\-\-ast"
must be given.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BR \-t ", \-\-tokens"
Print the token stream.
.TP
.BR \-p ", \-\-parser"
Print the parsed AST (pre-type-check).
.TP
.BR \-a ", \-\-ast"
Print the type-checked AST.
.RE
.TP
.BI transpile " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-\- " CC_FLAGS"]
Lex, parse, resolve, type-check, and transpile a .rl source file to C99.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-o ", \-\-output " PATH
Output .c path. Defaults to FILE with its extension changed to .c.
.TP
.B \-\-runtime
Also emit rl_runtime.h and rl_runtime.c.
.TP
.BR \-c ", \-\-compile"
After transpiling, invoke cc to compile the .c file.
.TP
.BI \-\-opt " LEVEL
Optimization level forwarded to cc (O0, O1, O2, O3, Os, Og).
Defaults to O2 when --compile is used.
.RE
.TP
.BI package " FILE"
.RI [ \-o " OUTPUT"]
Package a .rl file into a self-contained binary.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-o ", \-\-output " PATH
Output binary path. Defaults to "program".
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Compile to .rlc bytecode first and embed that instead of raw source text.
.RE
.TP
.B repl
Start the interactive TUI REPL with syntax highlighting and history.
.TP
.B lsp
Start the Language Server Protocol server over stdio.
.TP
.BI docs " TOPIC"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Print language reference and stdlib documentation. With no TOPIC, prints
everything. With a TOPIC, searches names across all categories.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Browse docs in an interactive terminal UI.
.TP
.B \-\-website
Open docs in a web browser.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print output as JSON instead of Markdown.
.TP
.B \-\-stdlib
Restrict search to stdlib docs.
.TP
.B \-\-concept
Restrict search to concept docs.
.TP
.B \-\-tutorial
Restrict search to tutorial docs.
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-file " PATH
Write output to a file instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-generate
Generate docs for current project.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Emit an HTML version of the generated site.
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-dir " PATH
Output directory for --generate.
.RE
.TP
.BI workflows " OPTIONS"
Scaffold GitHub Actions workflow files. At least one of
.B --check
or
.B --package
must be given.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-check
Generate a workflow that runs
.B rl check
on push/PR.
.TP
.B \-\-package
Generate a workflow that packages and releases a binary.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RL_VARIANT
Comma-separated list of variants for non-interactive install script use.
.TP
.B RL_VERSION
Version to install for non-interactive install script use.
.TP
.B RL_INSTALL_DIR
Installation directory for the install script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B rl.toml
Project configuration file read by
.BR "rl dev" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a script:
.RS
.PP
rl run hello.rl
.RE
.PP
Run with arguments:
.RS
.PP
rl run script.rl -- --verbose input.txt
.RE
.PP
Run inline code:
.RS
.PP
rl run -c 'println("hello")'
.RE
.PP
Start the REPL:
.RS
.PP
rl repl
.RE
.PP
Type-check a file:
.RS
.PP
rl check script.rl
.RE
.PP
Create a new project:
.RS
.PP
rl new my_project
.RE
.PP
Transpile to C:
.RS
.PP
rl transpile script.rl --runtime --compile
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (type errors, I/O failures, etc.).
